{
"about": "THE CONTENT PIPELINE'S BOARD/PAPER TABLE (tools/content.js). One row a family of papers, matched by paper_id prefix: its board, its qualification (the label in expected-papers.json; a family with one takes its board, subject, level and exam board from that line and its key stage from settings.json levels, never copied here: tools/one-list.js), the card fields every row of it carries, and where its transcription modules are. A new board or qualification is a new row here, never code. docs/notes/tools/content.md.",
"sources": {
"about": "THE ONE IMPORTER'S SOURCES (UNIFY NEXT 5, 22 Nov): each source a step list, run in order by `node tools/content.js <source> …`; the steps' shared parts (fetch, split, text, figures, write the cards, write the words, pack for the Ledger) live once in tools/lib/import.js.",
"paper": {"steps": ["source", "spec", "parts", "figures", "keys", "card", "import"], "what": "a past paper or worksheet: a transcription module, a family, library:<paper_id> or a spec"},
"markscheme": {"steps": ["cells", "answers", "words"], "what": "an AQA mark scheme: each row's answer from its own cell (aqa-ms-cells), applied to the words with --apply"},
"keypack": {"steps": ["validate", "apply"], "what": "a version-1 key pack (lib-import-*.json): checked by the backend's own libPackCheck_, then its fields set on the words"},
"insert": {"steps": ["sheets", "write"], "what": "the formulae and equation sheets (tools/inserts.py), written into data/inserts.json beside the reading inserts"},
"ideas": {"steps": ["measure", "merge", "tag"], "what": "one card per idea across levels (queue steps 10 and 3): each group of the same idea merged into one card, levels as tags, broad chapters split by point, every word kept; the report into data/settings/taxonomy.json Maths.ideas (with merged: old key -> card kept), then part_of, specs and idea_id onto the maths cards of data/textbooks.json (tools/lib/ideas.js)"},
"sets": {"steps": ["measure", "convert", "write"], "what": "one question set (UNIFY THE LIBRARY AND PRACTICE, item 3): every paper, worksheet, exercise and 5-a-day one kind, document_type the one word Question set, the source and sitting tags; a question carries no kind word, and a paper whose questions had no set row gets one; --apply writes data/questions.json (tools/lib/sets.js)"},
"speccode": {"steps": ["derive", "write"], "what": "spec_code on the papers whose code their own columns determine (the AQA June 2023 three; Edexcel GCSE maths 1MA1/<paper><tier>), a cell typed from a cover kept; --apply writes data/questions.json (was tools/set-spec-codes.py)"},
"sciideas": {"steps": ["measure", "merge", "tag"], "what": "one card per idea, science (UNIFY THE LIBRARY AND PRACTICE, item 8): an idea is one AQA spec point (8461, 8462, 8463; 8464 Combined shares them); a broad GCSE chapter's items go each to the point card they read most like, every word kept; the report into data/settings/taxonomy.json Science.ideas (merged: old key -> card kept), then part_of, specs and idea_id onto the science cards of data/textbooks.json (tools/lib/sci-ideas.js)"},
"qideas": {"steps": ["measure", "write"], "what": "one topic tree, maths and science (UNIFY THE LIBRARY AND PRACTICE, items 7 and 8): each maths and GCSE science question's idea_id, the idea it tests, read from data/settings/question-ideas.json (a set's idea, else its first listed topic's), and the ideas' names into data/settings/taxonomy.json Maths.ideaNames for Find's topic question (tools/lib/qideas.js; held by tools/one-topic.js); --apply writes"}
},
